    skos:prefLabel 'mole_fraction_of_acetaldehyde_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Mole fraction is used in the construction "mole_fraction_of_X_in_Y", where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as "nitrogen" or a phrase such as "nox_expressed_as_nitrogen". The chemical formula for acetaldehyde is CH3CHO. The IUPAC name for acetaldehyde is ethanal.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::UBNDM2MJ'^^xsd:string .
